  "img": "icons/sundries/gaming/card-astronomy-pink.webp",
  "description": "<p>Cartomancer: Roll a d12 when you lay out your reading, use Draw for the querent or use Read the room. A card's meaning takes effect on one creature: you, or the ally you turn it for. \"Their next\" means before the end of their next turn.</p><p>The Thirteenth is never rolled. It enters your reading only through a Ruin, a feat or a power. It is black and blank and cannot be turned by you. Once before your next Long Rest, the Dark Master may turn it at any moment: you or an ally within 30' makes one test with Bane. Then it is spent.</p>",
